ANSIBLE (Automation & Configuration Drift Scenarios)

These are real-life automation failures and recovery scenarios commonly asked in DevOps interviews.

⸻

🤖 Ansible – Real-World DevOps Scenarios
 1. An Ansible playbook runs successfully, but changes are not applied. How do you troubleshoot?
 2. A playbook works on one server but fails on another. What could be the reasons?
 3. How do you detect and fix configuration drift using Ansible?
 4. A playbook partially executed and failed in the middle. How do you recover safely?
 5. Secrets are hardcoded in playbooks. How do you fix this securely?
 6. Ansible execution is slow across many hosts. How do you optimize performance?
 7. A service restarted unexpectedly during a playbook run. How do you prevent downtime?
 8. How do you manage different environments (dev, qa, prod) in Ansible?
 9. An Ansible module is deprecated and breaks automation. How do you handle it?
 10. SSH authentication fails during playbook execution. How do you debug?
 11. How do you implement idempotency in Ansible playbooks?
 12. Logs are insufficient to debug a failed run. How do you improve observability?
 13. A configuration change caused a production outage. How do you roll back using Ansible?
 14. How do you integrate Ansible with CI/CD pipelines?
 15. How do you scale Ansible for hundreds or thousands of servers?

